 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 618342,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "Cytochrome c is an important component of the electron transport chain, a part of cellular respiration, and it is normally located in the cellular organelle, the mitochondrion. This protein has a heme prosthetic group, and the heme's central ion alternately reduces and oxidizes during electron transfer. Because this essential protein’s role in producing cellular energy is crucial, it has changed very little over millions of years. Protein sequencing has shown that there is a considerable amount of cytochrome c amino acid sequence homology among different species. In other words, we can assess evolutionary kinship by measuring the similarities or differences among various species’ DNA or protein sequences.",
   "stem_html": "Cytochrome c oxidase is a highly conserved protein found in bacteria and in the mitochondria of eukaryotes. Based on your knowledge of evolutionary relationships, which of the following statements would you expect to be true of the cytochrome c oxidase protein sequence?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1176714,
     "content_html": "The bacterial protein will be more similar to the human protein than the yeast protein."
    },
    {
     "id": 1176715,
     "content_html": "The yeast protein will be more similar to the human protein than the bacterial protein."
    },
    {
     "id": 1176713,
     "content_html": "The bacterial protein will be more similar to the yeast protein than the human protein."
    },
    {
     "id": 1176712,
     "content_html": "The bacterial and yeast proteins will share a similar sequence, but the human protein will be unrelated."
    }
   ],
